<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Citadelle Laferrière</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1805–<a href="/years/1820">1820</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Citadelle Henry</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Citadelle Laferrière is a mountaintop fortress near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milot">Milot</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haiti">Haiti</a>, built between about 1805 and 1820 by many thousands of workers on the orders of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henri-christophe">Henri Christophe</a>. It was designed to resist an expected French attempt to reconquer Haiti and was armed with scores of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/field-artillery">cannon</a>. With the Sans-Souci palace and the Ramiers buildings it forms a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a>, inscribed in 1982.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/citadelle-laferriere.jpg" alt="Citadelle Laferrière" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rémi Kaupp · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Citadelle_Laferri%C3%A8re.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
